# Assessment derivation - EFMP-302 Unit 4, G3 feat023-r1
# Reviewer: agent:g3-reviewer (fresh session; did not author or translate these bytes)
# Method: all 25 items solved from the unit content BEFORE the "## Answers and marking
# guidance" section (unit-assessment.mdx:178-303) was read, and before any prior report
# was read. Derived answers and the passage each rests on, then compared with the key.

## MCQ - derived blind

1. b   - topic-01 "### The concept of a professional standard": "A professional standard
         answers *what does competent teaching look like, in a form that can be checked?*"
         (a) is the code of conduct's question, (c) the curriculum's, (d) no document's.
2. d   - topic-01 three features: written / shared / "specific enough to be evidenced";
         "Be a good teacher" fails the third. Could be written and shared and still fail.
3. a   - topic-04 "### What happens when...": "a framework and an instrument built for
         continuing development were repurposed for accountability" = use mismatch.
4. c   - topic-02: "issued by the Ministry of Education, Government of Pakistan, in 2009,
         developed with support from UNESCO and USAID".
5. b   - topic-02: knowledge and understanding; dispositions; performance and skills.
6. d   - topic-02's three graded attempts: (a) not observable, (b) proxy satisfiable in an
         afternoon, (d) observable, hard to fake, tied to the standard. (c) seating plan is
         the added distractor, same proxy family as (b).
7. c   - topic-03: "a judgement formed first will select the evidence that confirms it.
         Kashif counted before he concluded."
8. a   - topic-03 evidence types: planning documents "are the easiest of all to produce
         without the underlying competence".
9. b   - topic-04: "Licensing asks *is this person currently fit to practise?*"
10. c  - topic-04: a teacher "will resolve the conflict rationally, by treating it as
         summative, because that is the version with consequences".

Comparison with the supplied key (unit-assessment.mdx:182-197): 10 of 10 agree.
No stem is ambiguous; each distractor is defensibly wrong on the unit's own terms.
Checked specifically: MCQ-06 (d) vs (b) - (b) is the unit's own named "proxy trap";
MCQ-04 - no distractor offers 2008, so the in-bundle 2008/2009 divergence (carried
advisory) harms no candidate.

## RRQ - derived expectations, then schemes checked for sum and stem-fit

RRQ-01 (4): three questions (prepared / currently fit / how doing) + why certificate and
    licence can disagree (past-preparation vs present-fitness judgement). Scheme 1+1+1+1=4. OK.
RRQ-02 (7): question + governs per instrument (2x3) + one real difference (scope,
    granularity, stakes). Scheme 2+2+2+1=7. OK.
RRQ-03 (8): four uses named (4) + apt requirement each (3) + one real tension (1).
    Scheme 4+3+1=8, sums; CARRIED ADVISORY CONFIRMED: the scheme pays "one mark per apt
    requirement (3)" then lists four requirements (initial training / development /
    appraisal / accountability), so a marker has no rule for which one goes unpaid.
RRQ-04 (4): candour vs candour-cost; trusted vs distant; weakness vs strength; must settle
    in advance which purpose each conversation carries. Scheme 1+1+1+1=4. OK. The "do not
    award" note matches topic-04's Isore wording (conflicting but not incompatible).
RRQ-05 (5): ten standards (1); three internal parts (2); indicators beneath parts (1);
    mixture of kinds so not parallel (1). Scheme 1+2+1+1=5. OK. The run-006 blocking defect
    stays repaired: the added clause is taught (topic-02 "### The domains the standards
    cover" + Summary + unit summary), duplicates neither RRQ-06 (what the separation buys)
    nor RRQ-07 (three tests of an indicator), and fig-U4-3's caption now agrees with the
    prose without the undisclosed frequency claim.
RRQ-06 (4): three distinct shortfalls (2); different remedies (1); single judgement hides
    which applies (1). Scheme 2+1+1=4. OK.
RRQ-07 (5): observable / specific / achievable (3); easy indicators measure proxies (1);
    proxies producible without competence (1). Scheme 3+1+1=5. OK.
RRQ-08 (9): five stations (5); two break points (2); why each defeats the comparison (2).
    Scheme 5+1+1+1+1=9. OK.
RRQ-09 (9): 3 marks per evidence type x 3. Allocation rule only; CARRIED ADVISORY
    CONFIRMED: no model content for any evidence type, against the blueprint's "each with a
    model answer and a point-by-point mark scheme". Mitigation stands: stem says "any
    three" and topic-03 "### Building evidence against an indicator" supplies the content.
RRQ-10 (4): won't bring a problem to someone who reports on them (1); mentoring is the
    cheapest effective development mechanism (1); loss invisible (1); appearance without
    function (1). Scheme 1+1+1+1=4. OK.

All ten schemes sum to their stated totals (4,7,8,4,5,4,5,9,9,4 = 59).

## ERQ - rubric shape

Five items, one per topic plus the integrative ERQ-02 (map the described teacher to
standards and parts, argue the appraisal consequence - matches the content-spec's summative
blueprint line). Each carries a four-criterion analytic rubric out of 20 with Limited /
Adequate / Strong bands, and the 10-mark cap below Adequate on the analysis, evaluation or
creation criterion is stated once for all five (unit-assessment.mdx:257-258). Rubrics
distinguish performance (e.g. ERQ-1 "Concedes the risk that evidence favours the compliant
and locates what in the design does or does not prevent it"). Demand labels: Evaluate,
Analyze, Create, Evaluate, Evaluate - all Analyze-or-higher as the blueprint requires.

## Bloom labels classified from the thinking required

MCQ band 3 Remember / 5 Understand / 2 Apply holds except MCQ-06, whose three options are
topic-02's own worked attempts in near-verbatim order - recognition for a reader of the
topic, so the *(Apply)* label overstates it (carried advisory; blueprint satisfied either
way). RRQ band: 7 Understand / 3 Analyze; the three Analyze items (04, 07, 10) are the ones
whose marks are mostly explanation, so the labels are honest. Recall-weighting pattern
across the RRQ band re-derived: roughly 43 of 59 marks pay for naming/listing/describing
taught content (e.g. RRQ-05 pays 4 of 5 for recitation; RRQ-09 is wholly descriptive) -
carried advisory, deferred to the bank-wide rebalancing pass in specs/backlog.md.
